            <zone forceUpdate='true' h='10000' id='251' type-v2='text' w='87750' x='11583' y='18125'>
              <formatted-text>
                <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>*Colour of the bars in Loss Measure Contribution indicate whether the segments are performing better than the </run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10' italic='true' underline='true'>country average.</run>
                <run fontsize='10' italic='true'> The darker the colour, the more positively/negatively performing it is. </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#93d07b' fontsize='10' italic='true' underline='true'>Green: Positive</run>
                <run fontcolor='#93d07b' fontsize='10' italic='true'>Æ </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d74246' fontsize='10' italic='true' underline='true'>Red: Negative</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>**Loss Measure Contribution indicates a </run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10' italic='true' underline='true'>contribution to metric loss </run>
                <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>(i.e. a positive value indicates that the metric decreased)</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>***Colour of the bars in Dynamic Measure indicates whether the segments are performing better than the </run>
                <run bold='true' fontsize='10' italic='true' underline='true'>previous week.</run>
                <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>Æ </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#3f6497' fontsize='10' italic='true' underline='true'>Blue: Positive</run>
                <run fontcolor='#3f6497' fontsize='10' italic='true'>Æ </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#a97300' fontsize='10' italic='true' underline='true'>Brown: Negative</run>
